    "methods_description": "Participants viewed representative subsets of THINGS images across 12 sessions while MEG was recorded. Images were presented in rapid succession (1.5±0.2s) with participants maintaining central fixation. An oddball detection task with artificially-generated images was used to maintain engagement. A subset of 200 images were repeated in each session. T1-weighted MRI scans were acquired for cortical source localization, and eye movements were monitored to verify fixation compliance.",
